+# Court foundation for the four flight exhibits and transcript access
+
+November 9, 2026. TEL02–TEL04 / AUD016-A1. Scope is the documentary foundation for the telephone portions of four multi-subject trial exhibits. Earlier event-level accounts and values are carried forward as unresolved.
+
+## What the records say
+
+The Eastern District of Virginia prosecution exhibit index lists **ST00004** under Phase 2. The public scan’s first page displays the exhibit stamp, the title *Stipulations for Part II of the Penalty Phase*, an **UNDER SEAL** face marking and a footnote limiting these stipulations to the second part of the penalty phase while also admitting the first-part stipulations there. The exhibit index and current public release page are separate access observations. The underlying order or exact change in seal status was outside this review. [Public court scan](https://coop.vaed.uscourts.gov/moussaoui/exhibits/prosecution/ST00004.pdf) · [Court prosecution index](https://coop.vaed.uscourts.gov/moussaoui/exhibits/prosecution.html) · [Court exhibit release, lines 30–35](https://www.vaed.uscourts.gov/node/150)
+
+| Stipulation locator | Exhibit | Subject in the four selected clauses |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| ¶21, printed p. 8 | P200018, Flight 11 | Crew identification, seat assignments and telephone calls |
+| ¶22, printed pp. 8–9 | P200019, Flight 175 | Crew identification, seat assignments and telephone calls |
+| ¶34, printed p. 11 | P200054, Flight 77 | Crew identification, seat assignments and telephone calls |
+| ¶36, printed p. 11 | P200055, Flight 93 | Crew identification, seat assignments and telephone calls |
+
+All four clauses stipulate to the authenticity of the **“underlying documents that support the admission”** of the named exhibit without further foundation. The selected clauses give exhibit IDs for the summary presentations. They leave the underlying source files, individual carrier records, dates, field definitions and call-to-record mappings unspecified. Adjacent ¶37 uses exhibit-level authenticity wording for P200056, the Flight 93 recorder presentation. These are distinct objects of the parties’ stipulations. [ST00004, printed pp. 8–9 and 11](https://coop.vaed.uscourts.gov/moussaoui/exhibits/prosecution/ST00004.pdf)
+
+The two court descriptions for P200054 and P200055 identify separate flight summaries, each offered as a roughly 27 MB Flash ZIP and each described as also covering the other three flights. This review compared the descriptions. Archive contents and byte identity remain untested. [P200054, lines 5–8](https://coop.vaed.uscourts.gov/moussaoui/exhibits/prosecution/flights/P200054.html) · [P200055, lines 5–8](https://coop.vaed.uscourts.gov/moussaoui/exhibits/prosecution/flights/P200055.html)
+
+The NPS history discusses credit-card records and states, **“These phone records were entered as evidence during the sentencing trial of Zacarias Moussaoui in 2006.”** Retain that statement alongside ST00004's language about supporting documents and the court index’s descriptions of presentations. The NPS paragraph gives no item IDs for the particular underlying records. The court clauses leave unresolved which underlying items were separately offered, admitted or displayed. The sources describe different aspects of the evidence and leave the relationship between them open. [NPS, opening account, line 23](https://www.nps.gov/flni/learn/historyculture/phone-calls-from-flight-93.htm) · [ST00004 ¶36](https://coop.vaed.uscourts.gov/moussaoui/exhibits/prosecution/ST00004.pdf)
+
+## Transcript labels and responses
+
+The official docket labels the April 25 entries redacted transcripts and the May 2 entries transcripts for the same three session labels. Followed all six links through the public court reader. Each returned one page beginning **“Transcripts are not available through this website.”** The notice identifies the clerk’s file as a route for unsealed hearing transcripts. Retain docket labels and notice contents separately. The page-count result applies to the online link responses. It establishes neither the length nor the actual content of the transcripts on file. Session selection was a bounded retrieval check. These docket labels alone give no exhibit offer, admission, display or transcript page for the four summaries. [Court docket, lines 105–107 and 121–123](https://coop.vaed.uscourts.gov/moussaoui/dktsheets/DocketSheet1.html)
+
+| Session as dated in docket | Volume | April 25 entries | May 2 entries |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| April 11, 2006, 9:30 a.m. | XVII | [1822](https://coop.vaed.uscourts.gov/moussaoui/dktsheets/docs/72332/0.pdf) | [1832](https://coop.vaed.uscourts.gov/moussaoui/dktsheets/docs/72372/0.pdf) |
+| April 11, 2006, 1:30 p.m. | XVII-A | [1823](https://coop.vaed.uscourts.gov/moussaoui/dktsheets/docs/72335/0.pdf) | [1833](https://coop.vaed.uscourts.gov/moussaoui/dktsheets/docs/72375/0.pdf) |
+| April 12, 2006 | XVIII | [1824](https://coop.vaed.uscourts.gov/moussaoui/dktsheets/docs/72338/0.pdf) | [1834](https://coop.vaed.uscourts.gov/moussaoui/dktsheets/docs/72378/0.pdf) |
+
+## Verification and remaining work
+
+The NPS page and court release page were downloaded anonymously, saved locally and matched to both recorded SHA-256 values and three text anchors. The PDF reader exposed selected text from the 16-page ST00004 scan, including the continuation of ¶22 and adjacent ¶37. Four exhibit/paragraph pairs and their foundation wording matched the retained reader extracts. All six single-page notices and three docket pairs were checked against the returned reader metadata. This comparison tests document wording and source relationships. It supplies no native routing, clock or carrier-event test.
+
+Direct local retrieval of the court’s exhibit host encountered a DNS failure. The old public path on the current court site returned HTTP 404. PDF bytes, hashes and signature-page inspection remain unavailable for the court scan and notices. The direct HTML hashes and reader locators are separately identified in the source pins. A reader rendering is a distinct source representation.
+
+- **TODO TEL02.** Obtain the complete ST00004 scan bytes, verify the execution and filing context, and seek the itemized trial exhibit inventory or trial transcript pages showing the offer, admission or display. Use the docket’s exact session locators only as candidates until a page-level match. Keep carrier documents supporting admission and documents separately introduced in evidence as separate questions.
+- **TODO TEL03–TEL04.** Obtain call-specific carrier/operator records and the worksheet that maps them to a specific exhibit screen. Test the service, attempt/connection/duration, clocks, caller and transfer/recipient joins only with those inputs. The zero-duration row’s meaning, Keyton record chain and native usage-report chain remain open.
+- **Earlier conflicts.** This foundation review supplies no new event-level value. Preserve the early office-connection account and later no-connection description, the seven/eight entries and the 154/159 duration values at their original scopes. [Earlier usage-report review](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/5031c6dfa73e1f59491f259e00f168c37cb21788/investigation/broader-evidence/telephone-usage-report-2026-10-27/README.md)
